85 true] [17592186405147 1074 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)={y}^{2}-2$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper cone ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP={z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,Q=0,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})-(0)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the lower cylinder ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-2)=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-2)=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP={z}^{2}={({y}^{2}-2)}^{2},\\,Q=0,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is downward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂h}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-{({y}^{2}-2)}^{2}\\cdot (0)+0\\cdot (2y)+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405149 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405150 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405151 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405152 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405153 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1077 "selection" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1079 #edb/ref 17592186405153 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405148 1080 #uuid "ae335d47-3b07-5474-9957-6ab74654f8ab" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405149 1081 "\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-2y" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405149 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405149 1084 #uuid "0cefe31a-522d-5318-b0c1-4892165c8d4d" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405150 1081 "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405150 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405150 1084 #uuid "6dbfd4cf-3634-5dbd-b50c-a2a6baa15297" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405151 1081 "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+x" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405151 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405151 1084 #uuid "b0d797f0-c71c-527a-a6dd-aeedb88fb5db" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405152 1081 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405152 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405152 1084 #uuid "1a998466-68ff-5ef7-bee3-792b48a2d00f" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405153 1081 "x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405153 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405153 1084 #uuid "265f91a3-d619-5622-b9e3-15ca49b4b395" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1068 #edb/ref 17592186405155 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1069 "q-32876" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1071 "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2}),$ valid for real values of $u?$" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1072 #uuid "33bfb8ae-51e5-575a-aee2-202f3434e957" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1074 "The point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r({t}_{0})+u\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t=-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t=0 \\\\ t=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $t=\\frac{3}{2}.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of the vector $r(\\frac{3}{2}).$  \n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=\\frac{3}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u\\,(\\pi \\,j+\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405156 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405157 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405158 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405159 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405160 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1077 "selection" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1079 #edb/ref 17592186405158 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405155 1080 #uuid "cc1f347e-fe06-5ef7-a082-5d1425a121dd" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405156 1081 "-i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,i+\\,k)" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405156 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405156 1084 #uuid "109c8716-781f-5d87-93da-32c8a82a52af" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405157 1081 "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,i+\\,j)" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405157 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405157 1084 #uuid "2a44